---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';

const redesignPaperHref = withBase('/research/executable-evidence-public-resumes.pdf');
const researchPaperHref = withBase('/research/verifiable-web-artifacts.pdf');
const flexModelHref = withBase('/research/FlexFacets.tla');
---

<section id="case-studies" class="case-studies" aria-labelledby="case-studies-title">
  <div class="case-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">05 / Case studies</p>
    <h2 id="case-studies-title">The method, tested in practice.</h2>
    <p>
      These public projects show the reasoning in context: one turns a design problem into
      an engineering loop; the other tests the limits of the guarantees that loop can offer.
      They are examples of how I work, not claims about every system I build.
    </p>
  </div>

  <article id="case-redesign" class="case-study" aria-labelledby="redesign-title">
    <header class="case-heading">
      <p class="mono-label">Case 01 · Engineering</p>
      <h3 id="redesign-title">Turn a subjective redesign into testable decisions.</h3>
      <p class="case-context">A public website redesign, studied across 18 commits.</p>
      <a class="study-link" href={redesignPaperHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        Read the redesign case study <Icon name="file" size={16} />
      </a>
    </header>

    <dl class="case-story">
      <div>
        <dt>Challenge</dt>
        <dd>A legacy résumé site needed a clearer reading order without losing approved
          information. “Make it look better” was too vague to guide or evaluate changes.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Approach</dt>
        <dd>I separated the content from its presentation, turned alignment and readability
          feedback into browser checks, and used focused edits followed by build and
          deployment verification.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Finding</dt>
        <dd>In the original matched desktop study, first-fold words fell from
          <strong>262 to 91</strong>, and text elements smaller than 13px fell from
          <strong>27 to 0</strong>. These are historical presentation measurements,
          not a live score for this page or a measurement of hiring outcomes.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="case-lesson">
        <dt>Lesson</dt>
        <dd>Make intent concrete enough to test. A browser check can preserve a design
          decision, but passing tests does not replace reading the page as a person.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </article>

  <article id="case-verification" class="case-study" aria-labelledby="research-title">
    <header class="case-heading">
      <p class="mono-label">Case 02 · Bounded research result</p>
      <h3 id="research-title">Find where a verification claim stops.</h3>
      <p class="case-context">A follow-up manuscript on layout independence and disclosure auditing.</p>
      <a class="study-link" href={researchPaperHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        Read the research manuscript <Icon name="file" size={16} />
      </a>
    </header>

    <div class="research-body">
      <dl class="case-story">
        <div>
          <dt>Challenge</dt>
          <dd>A passing test is not the same as a general guarantee. I wanted to understand
            which layout and publication properties the available checks actually establish.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Approach</dt>
          <dd>I compared a finite layout model with exact calculations and browser probes,
            then checked one repository’s emitted content against an explicit disclosure policy.
            I also tested whether the instruments themselves could fail.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Finding</dt>
          <dd>The layout predicate covered fewer containers than the probes found apparently
            independent. The disclosure case exposed audit gaps. A generated-artifact
            feasibility run produced no scored formal result or quality gain, and ordinary
            deeper search matched the synthetic TLC witness.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="case-lesson">
          <dt>Lesson</dt>
          <dd>When review reveals that a conclusion goes beyond its evidence, narrow the
            conclusion. These studies do not establish a cost-effectiveness ranking or an
            artifact-quality benefit from formal feedback.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <details class="research-evidence">
        <summary>Evidence and limitations</summary>
        <div class="evidence-content">
          <p class="evidence-scope">Layout study · 1,200 pages · 2,255 eligible containers · six measured widths</p>
          <dl class="evidence-values">
            <div><dt>Containers with no coupling detected by finite probes</dt><dd>45.76%</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Containers whose items all satisfy the local predicate</dt><dd>28.07%</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p>
            The predicate is maximal on eight checked finite domains covering 3.5M
            configuration-item pairs, not proved maximal for arbitrary CSS. The browser
            figures depend on finite probes and pages rendered without external assets.
          </p>
          <p>
            The disclosure result is one self-audited repository with hand-assigned labels
            and flows; human authoring and maintenance time were not measured. A richer
            layout-information ladder, causal attribution, a disclosure mutation campaign,
            and independent replication remain research work, not completed findings.
          </p>
          <p>
            Study C tested one paid generated-artifact task. Its baseline received 58/100,
            while the formal arm blocked before repair and remained unscored after 13 provider
            requests. Offline harness fixes and synthetic traces are not benchmark results.
          </p>
          <a class="study-link" href={flexModelHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            Read the flexbox TLA+ model <Icon name="file" size={16} />
          </a>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </article>

  <p class="case-closing">
    <strong>The common thread:</strong> turn a challenge into a clear question, make a testable
    move, and let the result, not attachment to the original idea, determine what happens next.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .case-studies {
    padding: clamp(64px, 7vw, 96px) var(--gutter);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--panel);
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .case-intro {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .case-intro .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(30px, 3.3vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .case-intro > p:last-child {
    margin-top: 22px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 17px;
  }

  .case-study {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 72px);
    padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px);
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .case-study + .case-study {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .case-heading .mono-label {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 32px);
    line-height: 1.15;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .case-context {
    margin-top: 18px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .study-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    min-height: 44px;
    margin-top: 22px;
    color: var(--accent-strong);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .study-link :global(svg) {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .case-story {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .case-story > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 84px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 18px;
    padding-block: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .case-story > div:first-child {
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .case-story dt {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 650;
    padding-top: 2px;
  }

  .case-story dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .case-story strong,
  .case-lesson dt {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .case-story .case-lesson {
    border-top-color: var(--accent);
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .case-lesson dd {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .research-evidence {
    margin-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  summary {
    padding-block: 16px;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--accent-strong);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .evidence-content {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .evidence-content > p + p {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .evidence-scope {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .evidence-values {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin-block: 24px;
  }

  .evidence-values > div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .evidence-values dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 28px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .case-closing {
    margin-top: 40px;
    max-width: 86ch;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .case-closing strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .case-study {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .case-study {
      padding: 24px 20px;
    }

    .case-story > div {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 8px;
    }

    .evidence-values {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>